<p>Dallas homes are built with summer in mind. Supply lines run through attics over the garage, through exterior brick-veneer walls, and under older pier-and-beam floors where cold air moves freely. Most winters, a night or two below freezing passes without trouble. Then a storm like Uri settles in for days, the power flickers or fails, and pipes that have never had a problem split open. Freeze damage and burst pipe claims usually surface during the thaw, when water starts flowing again and ceilings start to sag.</p>

<p>This guide covers what the weather record shows for Dallas County, how burst pipe claims are typically handled, where these claims get disputed, and how to document a freeze loss so the insurer has what it needs to evaluate it. It is general information. Your policy language controls, and coverage always depends on the facts.</p>

