<tr><td>Opening walls or ceilings to reach the break</td><td>Often covered</td><td>Policy wording on tear-out and access</td></tr>
<tr><td>The cracked pipe or fitting itself</td><td>Varies by policy</td><td>Some policies exclude repair of the system that froze</td></tr>
<tr><td>Furniture, clothing, electronics, and other contents</td><td>Covered under personal property if the cause is covered</td><td>Actual cash value vs. replacement cost</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hotel and extra costs while the home is unlivable</td><td>Often covered as additional living expense</td><td>Limits and time frames; keep receipts</td></tr>
